  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.7250) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. The only major unexplored dimension in this proven architecture is the RNA encoder. Config_036 swaps scvi_n200 for scgpt while keeping all other settings at their best-known values (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). This directly tests whether a different learned RNA encoder can push accuracy beyond 0.7250 or confirm that scvi_n200 is near-optimal. If scgpt performs comparably, we gain confidence the RNA encoder is not the bottleneck; if it improves, we identify a new best. Expected cost is moderate (~4–5 GPU hours), similar to config_039's 3.60 h since the dominant cost drivers (ViT-L image encoder + transformer aggregation) are unchanged, with scgpt adding a modest overhead over scvi_n200. With 5 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information experiment that exploits the strongest evidence while exploring the largest untested design axis."
}

